      "description": "Watch Abha vs Al Hazem highlights and goals from Pro League - Saudi Arabia on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 13, 2026. The Pro League encounter on August 13, 2026 , between Abha and Al Hazem promised a fascinating tactical battle as both sides aimed to secure an early-season momentum boost. Abha's Lightning Start The match ignited almost immediately as the home side took control from the very first whistle. In the 3rd minute, Abdulaziz Al-Dwehe found the back of the net to give Abha an early lead, expertly assisted by Ahmed Al-Shamrani . This early breakthrough forced Al Hazem into a defensive shell, and their struggles to cope with the pace of the game led to a yellow card for Amine Ben Hamida in the 27th minute as the visitors tried to stem the tide of attacks. Doubling the Advantage As the first half drew to a close, Abha ’s persistent pressure paid off once again. In the 40th minute, Ahmed Al-Shamrani turned from provider to finisher, slotting home a clinical goal following a well-timed assist from Sofiane Bendebka . The half ended with a flurry of intensity, characterized by a yellow card for Bendebka just before the whistle, leaving the visitors with a mountain to climb in the second period. Clinical Finish and Strategic Changes The second half saw both managers turn to their benches to influence the flow of the game. Al Hazem introduced Nabil Fekir in hopes of finding a creative spark, but it was Abha 's substitute Basil Al-Sayyali who made the most significant impact. Just minutes after entering the field, Al-Sayyali scored in the 63rd minute to effectively end the contest. Despite late yellow cards for Feras Al-Ghamdi , Aboubacar Bah , and Loreintz Rosier , Abha remained composed, seeing out the final minutes to claim a well-deserved victory."
